# nitpick server config: the keys, never the values.
#
# Copy this file to a path outside the repo, fill it in there, and point
# NITPICK_CONFIG_FILE at it. Or set the same keys in the environment, which
# wins over the file. An empty value keeps the default.

# The address to listen on. Default: loopback only.
NITPICK_HOST=
# The port to listen on. Default: 4870.
NITPICK_PORT=
# At most this many devices booted at once, so the host's memory holds: 1 on
# an 8 GB host, 2 on a 16 GB one. A start that needs room shuts down devices
# nobody is reviewing on; past that, it names who is. Default: no cap.
NITPICK_MAX_BOOTED_DEVICES=
# Where the server keeps its data.
# Default: ~/Library/Application Support/nitpick-server
NITPICK_DATA_DIR=
# The one YouTrack instance Reviewers sign in to with their own permanent
# token, and file into. Required: the server doesn't start without it.
# Tokens never go in this file; each Reviewer's is kept encrypted in the data
# directory, under its sign-in-key file.
NITPICK_YOUTRACK_URL=
